instrument wingie
; wingie-proc-everything — five whole chains for line in, each grains into spectrum into time (or
; the other way round), with feedback from the end back to the start. Line/Mic switch to line.
;
; every scene:
;   fader1 (Mix)     how much the first stage does (density, speed, stretch)
;   fader2 (Decay)   how long the last stage holds (echo feedback, room, ring)
;   fader3 (Volume)  how much of the middle stage (spectral blend, freeze, colour)
;   keys1            the pitch of the grains; octave1 an octave down or up
;   keys2            the second hand: held, the spectrum freezes (or the resonance is struck)
;   key24 (top B)    the next scene;  key23 (top A#) the one before (no Mode combo needed)
;   mode1            held: the first stage stops time (freeze / hold)
;   mode2            tap: latch the feedback from the end back to the start
;   left LED         how loud the line in is;  right LED  what comes back round

the whole river
---------------
; grains of the line, pitched to the bottom keys and denser the louder you play, into a spectral
; freeze that any held top key stops, into a tape echo; tap mode2 and the echo runs back into the
; grains, so the river feeds itself.
the g is grains 2 samplerate=quarter window=hann spread=0.8
the ear is follower attack=0.01 release=0.4
the oct1 is transpose
the hang is specfreeze samplerate=quarter
the echo is tapeecho 1 time=0.8 wow=0.2 samplerate=quarter
the latch is flipflop
the back is vca
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> g ear
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> g.pitch
fader1 -> g.density
ear -40> g.density
mode1 -> g.freeze
g.left g.right -> hang
keys2.gate -> hang.freeze
fader3 -> hang.blend
hang -> echo
fader2 -> echo.feedback
echo.wet -> back
mode2.tap -> latch
latch => back.gain
back -35> g
hang -50> guard
echo -> guard
guard -> out
key24.trig -> scene.next
key23.trig -> scene.back
ear -> lights.left
echo.wet -> lights.right

stretch to glass
----------------
; the line slowed down without falling in pitch (fader1: up is as it was, down stands still),
; pitched by the bottom keys, into a room (fader3 how much goes in, fader2 its size). Hold mode1
; or a top key and the stretch loops where it is; tap mode2 and the room runs back into the stretch.
the slow is stretch 2 samplerate=quarter
the oct1 is transpose
the wet is vca
the room is reverblite 4
the latch is flipflop
the back is vca
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> slow
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> slow.pitch
fader1 -> slow.speed
mode1 -> slow.hold
slow -> wet -> room
keys2.gate -> slow.hold
fader3 -> wet.gain
fader2 -> room.size
room -> back
mode2.tap -> latch
latch => back.gain
back -30> slow
slow -40> guard
room -> guard
guard -> out
key24.trig -> scene.next
key23.trig -> scene.back
line.both -> lights.left
room -> lights.right

cave, glass, prism
------------------
; a Wingie cave rings on the line (the top keys strike it, fader3 how long it rings), grains
; read the ringing at the bottom keys' pitch (fader1 density), and a ping-pong echo throws the
; grains from side to side (fader2 the feedback). Tap mode2 and the echoes go back into the cave.
the cave is cave 2 samplerate=half
the g is grains 1 samplerate=half window=gauss spread=0.6
the oct1 is transpose
the bins is pingpong 4
the latch is flipflop
the back is vca
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> cave
keys2.trig -> cave.strike
fader3 -> cave.decay
cave -> g
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> g.pitch
fader1 -> g.density
mode1 -> g.freeze
g.left g.right -> bins
fader2 -> bins.feedback
bins.l bins.r -> back
mode2.tap -> latch
latch => back.gain
back -25> cave
cave -30> guardl guardr
g.left bins.l -> guardl
g.right bins.r -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
key24.trig -> scene.next
key23.trig -> scene.back
line.both -> lights.left
bins.l -> lights.right

the glacier
-----------
; the line stretched a thousand times (PaulStretch; fader1 how far: down is as it was), through a
; Wingie resonator tuned by the bottom keys and struck by the top keys (fader2 how long it rings),
; then shifted in frequency by fader3: the glacier slowly bends out of tune. mode1 stops time.
the ice is paulstretch 1 samplerate=quarter
the ring is wingie 2 samplerate=half shape=bar
the oct1 is transpose
the latch is flipflop
the back is vca
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> ice
fader1 -> ice.stretch
mode1 -> ice.hold
ice -> ring
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> ring.pitch
keys2.trig -> ring.strike
fader2 -> ring.decay
ring -> back
mode2.tap -> latch
latch => back.gain
back -20> ice
ice ring -50> guardl guardr
fader3 -> ring.strike
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
key24.trig -> scene.next
key23.trig -> scene.back
line.both -> lights.left
ring -> lights.right

the cathedral
-------------
; the line sung by a granular choir on a chord built on the bottom keys (octave1 moves it),
; fader1 how many voices; the choir goes into a long dark reverb (fader2 how long), and a held
; top key holds the reverb for ever, letting nothing new in. fader3 how dark. Tap mode2 and the
; reverb feeds the choir back.
the choir is harmonicgrains 2 samplerate=half chord=fifths size=0.2
the oct1 is transpose
the nave is cavern samplerate=quarter
the latch is flipflop
the back is vca
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> choir
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> choir.pitch
fader1 -> choir.density
choir.left choir.right -> nave
fader2 -> nave.size
fader3 -> nave.dark
keys2.gate mode1 -> nave.hold
nave.left -> back
mode2.tap -> latch
latch => back.gain
back -20> choir
choir.left nave.left -> guardl
choir.right nave.right -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
key24.trig -> scene.next
key23.trig -> scene.back
line.both -> lights.left
nave.left -> lights.right
